# Cloudflare Pages defaults to redirecting any extensionless path to its
# trailing-slash form (e.g. /experience -> /experience/ via 308) whenever it
# finds a matching directory+index.html in the build output. Gatsby's own
# `trailingSlash: "never"` config only affects the app's own generated links/
# canonicals/sitemap, not this platform-level behaviour — so left alone, the
# site permanently redirects away from the exact URLs it declares as
# canonical everywhere else. These rewrites (200, not a redirect) serve each
# page's content directly at its no-slash URL, pre-empting that default.
/acknowledgement /acknowledgement/index.html 200
/intro /intro/index.html 200
/experience /experience/index.html 200
/projects /projects/index.html 200
/education /education/index.html 200
/contact /contact/index.html 200
